    "narrative": "The ceiling for tonight\u2019s slate is firmly anchored by **Corbin Carroll**, whose 76.19 efficiency score stands as our premier play. Facing Michael McGreevy (xERA 4.43), **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a potent combination of a favorable SP matchup and a prime #3 hole projection, with his elite sprint speed providing the essential stolen base floor we prioritize in this league. Following him, **Vinnie Pasquantino** earns a strong 66.63 score, bolstered by a significant platoon advantage against the right-handed Troy Melton. Despite the park factor volatility, **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a set-and-forget anchor for the 1B slot, as his profile aligns perfectly with the need for high-efficiency run production.\n\nNavigating the remainder of the lineup required careful calibration. **Gabriel Moreno** edges into \"Strong\" territory at 60.15, though we are keeping a close eye on his lineup placement; should he shift out of the #4 spot, his utility diminishes slightly. Meanwhile, **Zach McKinstry** (55.54) and **Austin Riley** (53.73) land in our \"Marginal\" bucket. **Zach McKinstry** benefits immensely from a soft matchup against Randy Dobnak (xERA 5.65), which offset his lower batting order position, while **Austin Riley** remains a hold despite a tougher test against a left-handed arm. **Travis Bazzana** (47.51) rounds out the infield, capturing the last spot over our off-day cohort. \n\nThe bench remains static today as **Jose Caballero**, **Josh Naylor**, **James Wood**, and **Mickey Moniak** are all sidelined by team off-days, rendering them unavailable for rotation. With no viable bench threats for the active slots, the primary risk remains the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Zach McKinstry**, and **Corbin Carroll**. Should any of these players move down the order or face late-scratch conditions due to weather or rest, we are prepared to pivot to the high-upside depth on our taxi squad, including **Brice Turang** or **Seiya Suzuki**, should they be activated from their respective status windows. We are locked in for tonight\u2019s action, prioritizing aggressive base-running and high-xERA exploitation.",
